<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Leipzig</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of the Nations, Völkerschlacht · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-sixth-coalition">War of the Sixth Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a>, or Battle of the Nations, was fought on 16–19 October 1813 around Leipzig in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>. The armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> in a battle involving some 600,000 soldiers, and his German allies began to desert him. It was the largest battle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, ended French power east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and led to the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1814.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-leipzig.jpg" alt="Battle of Leipzig" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vladimir Moshkov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MoshkovVI_SrazhLeypcigomGRM.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Austria joined the Sixth Coalition in August 1813, and Field Marshal Karl Philipp zu Schwarzenberg commanded the Allied armies that won the <b>Battle of Leipzig</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The German Confederation (Deutscher Bund) was created at the Congress of Vienna to fill the space left by the Holy Roman Empire, dissolved in 1806, and by Napoleon’s Confederation of the Rhine, which had collapsed after the <b>Battle of Leipzig</b> in 1813.</blockquote><a href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Frederick abandoned Napoleon after the <b>Battle of Leipzig</b>, and by the Treaty of Fulda of November 1813 the Allies guaranteed his possessions, so that the kingdom survived the Congress of Vienna intact.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-wurttemberg">Kingdom of Württemberg · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>After his defeat at the <b>Battle of Leipzig</b>, Allied armies crossed Swiss territory in December 1813 and the Mediation regime collapsed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/swiss-confederation">Swiss Confederation · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>With some 600,000 soldiers engaged over three days, the '<b>Battle of the Nations</b>' was the largest in Europe before the First World War.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-16">16 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Battle of the Nations</b> ended with Napoleon's army in retreat from Leipzig, its rearguard trapped when a bridge was blown too early.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-19">19 October in history</a></li></ul></section>
